  "id": "DrugBank_DB04572 - MONDO_17327",
  "verbalization": "Thiotepa appears to be linked to Primary Non-gestational Choriocarcinoma Of Ovary through a shared pathway involving Altretamine, which is indicated in multiple contexts. The evidence suggests that Thiotepa may act as a mediator in the treatment of ovarian tumors, as it is associated with both Malignant Dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary and Immature Ovarian Teratoma, which both are indicated to interact with Altretamine. This indicates a potential mechanism where Thiotepa may influence the progression or treatment of these tumors by promoting the activity of Altretamine, which in turn affects the development of Primary Non-gestational Choriocarcinoma Of Ovary. The recurring association with Altretamine suggests a possible role in the biological pathways that underlie the development of this cancer, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a possible dependency on Altretamine, which may be a key component in the therapeutic or pathophysiological process of this condition.",
